WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.210 --> 00:00:01.767
- That's when I was like, "You know what?

00:00:01.767 --> 00:00:03.016
"Maybe you're gay."

00:00:03.016 --> 00:00:05.793
And little did I realize I am very gay.

00:00:10.960 --> 00:00:12.930
- We had an email at Buzzfeed asking us

00:00:12.930 --> 00:00:15.540
if there were any moments that
really defined our sexuality.

00:00:15.540 --> 00:00:18.200
Or, like, kind of made us
realize who we were inside.

00:00:18.200 --> 00:00:20.160
And, I hadn't really given it any thought.

00:00:20.160 --> 00:00:21.973
And then it (laughs) came to me.

00:00:22.580 --> 00:00:25.053
That scene where that very hot, tan,

00:00:25.330 --> 00:00:27.800
almost like Grecian, European looking guy.

00:00:27.800 --> 00:00:29.180
I can't remember whether
he reaches for his phone

00:00:29.180 --> 00:00:31.030
or if he reaches over, but he like...

00:00:31.420 --> 00:00:32.253
He reaches.

00:00:32.820 --> 00:00:34.370
I remember literally pausing it

00:00:34.420 --> 00:00:36.367
on the button on the DVD
and being like (gasps).

00:00:38.180 --> 00:00:39.163
Okay, play!

00:00:39.230 --> 00:00:40.063
And that was it.

00:00:40.063 --> 00:00:42.220
It was like a brief little
moment I had with myself.

00:00:42.220 --> 00:00:44.293
And I didn't touch myself
or anything like that.

00:00:44.293 --> 00:00:46.203
But it was like, "Hm,

00:00:46.924 --> 00:00:47.757
"that was nice."

00:00:47.757 --> 00:00:49.010
- You know that scene in Mulan

00:00:49.010 --> 00:00:50.410
where she chops off all her hair

00:00:50.410 --> 00:00:53.003
and becomes a badass member
of the (laughs) army.

00:00:53.450 --> 00:00:55.740
And just, like, defies
so many gender roles.

00:00:55.740 --> 00:00:57.040
That really did it for me.

00:00:57.090 --> 00:00:59.930
Realizing that I was attracted
to something so fluid

00:00:59.930 --> 00:01:03.060
kind of scared me, but
also it was super exciting.

00:01:03.060 --> 00:01:05.570
I was just shown something
that I hadn't ever seen before.

00:01:05.570 --> 00:01:07.070
Thank you Mulan (laughs)

00:01:07.070 --> 00:01:10.253
for helping this gay
baby heart find herself.

00:01:10.530 --> 00:01:11.980
- I think when I was six or seven,

00:01:11.980 --> 00:01:16.100
I was watching a Ricky Martin
concert on TV with my family.

00:01:16.100 --> 00:01:19.110
I distinctly remember him
singing Livin' La Vida Loca,

00:01:19.110 --> 00:01:21.147
his shirt was not on and
I remember being like,

00:01:21.147 --> 00:01:23.000
"Oh, okay."

00:01:23.000 --> 00:01:24.433
I still love Ricky Martin.

00:01:24.480 --> 00:01:26.240
It was actually a pretty cool moment

00:01:26.240 --> 00:01:27.600
for me when he came out.

00:01:27.600 --> 00:01:30.560
This is somebody that I grew
up admiring, I love his music.

00:01:30.560 --> 00:01:32.730
Seeing kind of your childhood icon,

00:01:32.730 --> 00:01:34.440
like, identify the same way that you do.

00:01:34.440 --> 00:01:36.100
- One of my pop culture moments

00:01:36.100 --> 00:01:38.370
was when I was watching
K.Will's Please Don't.

00:01:38.370 --> 00:01:40.073
It is a Korean pop music video.

00:01:40.210 --> 00:01:43.373
And it has like a huge plot
twist that I was not ready for.

00:01:43.420 --> 00:01:45.180
It seems like the director was shooting

00:01:45.180 --> 00:01:47.133
as if the guy was jealous of the girl.

00:01:47.160 --> 00:01:50.080
Crazy thing is, the guy actually
is falling for the groom.

00:01:50.080 --> 00:01:51.663
And it was, like, mind blowing!

00:01:52.320 --> 00:01:54.970
I was like, "Whoa, so
all this time he's gay?"

00:01:54.970 --> 00:01:58.113
As a person of color, as a
person that's from Asian descent,

00:01:58.400 --> 00:02:00.680
this is a topic that we
don't really approach

00:02:00.680 --> 00:02:01.720
and we don't talk about.

00:02:01.720 --> 00:02:03.920
There's not much
representation in these roles.

00:02:03.920 --> 00:02:05.660
So, to see someone that looked like me,

00:02:05.660 --> 00:02:07.637
that has similar skin color as me

00:02:07.637 --> 00:02:09.800
and has same facial structure as me,

00:02:09.800 --> 00:02:12.860
that helped me, in terms
of who I think gay is,

00:02:12.860 --> 00:02:15.743
what gay means, to who I am.

00:02:16.110 --> 00:02:19.840
- So, my gay awakening
occurred when I was watching

00:02:19.840 --> 00:02:22.260
Brokeback Mountain with my parents.

00:02:22.260 --> 00:02:25.830
This fairly explicit gay sex scene

00:02:25.830 --> 00:02:27.740
was just, like, kind of happening.

00:02:27.740 --> 00:02:30.507
I was like, "Oh, what's going on here?"

00:02:30.550 --> 00:02:34.340
Seeing an example of gay intimacy

00:02:34.380 --> 00:02:37.200
on screen and realizing
that that was something

00:02:37.200 --> 00:02:40.440
I was curious and fascinated
by and interested in.

00:02:40.440 --> 00:02:43.050
Was, like, immediately
paired with a moment

00:02:43.050 --> 00:02:45.480
of my parents telling me that

00:02:45.500 --> 00:02:48.140
what I had just started to see was bad.

00:02:48.140 --> 00:02:49.310
They made me leave the room.

00:02:49.310 --> 00:02:50.820
And, for the record, my parents let me

00:02:50.820 --> 00:02:52.370
watch straight sex scenes.

00:02:52.370 --> 00:02:54.153
So, it wasn't just that
it was a sex scene.

00:02:54.153 --> 00:02:55.873
It's that it was a gay sex scene.

00:02:55.900 --> 00:02:58.530
I think before watching the
sex scene in Brokeback Mountain

00:02:58.530 --> 00:03:00.280
I did know that I was gay,

00:03:00.280 --> 00:03:02.200
but it wasn't something
that I was cognizant of.

00:03:02.200 --> 00:03:05.000
It was something that was
definitely a little repressed.

00:03:05.000 --> 00:03:07.070
Watching that scene helped
me realize something

00:03:07.070 --> 00:03:09.833
that I already knew, but was
afraid to admit to myself.

00:03:10.140 --> 00:03:13.470
- There's not really that many,
like, lesbian iconic moments

00:03:13.470 --> 00:03:16.490
that made me realize, like,
this is also, too, how I feel.

00:03:16.490 --> 00:03:19.500
Any time there was, like,
a strong female lead

00:03:19.520 --> 00:03:22.160
on whatever I was watching, I
would just be like obsessed.

00:03:22.160 --> 00:03:23.927
And be like, "Oh my god, I love her.

00:03:23.927 --> 00:03:24.973
"Not in a gay way.

00:03:25.127 --> 00:03:26.850
"But also in a gay way, probably."

00:03:26.850 --> 00:03:28.470
I'm pretty sure baby me

00:03:28.470 --> 00:03:31.223
had a huge crush on Carmen from Spy Kids.

00:03:31.410 --> 00:03:33.700
Girl was resourceful, so intense

00:03:33.700 --> 00:03:35.740
and so just, like, true to who she is.

00:03:35.740 --> 00:03:37.510
But, at the end of the
day, is just like a softy

00:03:37.510 --> 00:03:38.910
and, like, just wants to take care of Juni

00:03:38.910 --> 00:03:40.350
and his weird wart fingers.

00:03:40.350 --> 00:03:41.540
And like, I don't know,

00:03:41.540 --> 00:03:43.440
I think she's a really cool character.

00:03:43.670 --> 00:03:45.777
It's so weird to, like,
look back and be like,

00:03:45.777 --> 00:03:48.677
"Those are such gay things
going through your head."

